course: dictionary
lesson: 14945
title: Words with a hidden meaning: re-
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts. The start of a word, called a prefix, can change its meaning. Re- at the start of a word often means again or back. «The rangers will reintroduce beavers to the river next spring.» The word around it, next spring, tells you the beavers have not been there for a while.
explain: To reintroduce means to bring something back to a place or a use it had before. Introduce means to bring in something for the first time, so reintroduce adds the idea of again. Think of re- as a sign that says: this has been here before.
explain: Reintroduce can be about animals and plants, or about things people do. «Our head teacher wants to reintroduce the old reading rule.» The rule was used before, then stopped, and now it is coming back. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does «bring back the old reading rule» still make sense? If it does, you have it.
fact: Re- at the start of a word often means again or back.
fact: To reintroduce means to bring back, either an animal or plant to a place where it used to live, or something like a rule back into use.
fact: «Reintroduce» is made of re- (again) and introduce (bring in for the first time).
fact: You can reintroduce an animal into the wild, which means setting it free in nature again.
fact: Other words with re- work the same way: «rewrite» means write again, and «replay» means play again.
exercise: «The rangers will reintroduce beavers to the river next spring.» What does reintroduce mean here? | *To bring back animals to a place where they used to live | To count how many beavers there are | To move animals to a new country for the first time | To chase animals away from the river
exercise: «Our head teacher wants to reintroduce the old reading rule.» What is being brought back? | A teacher from another school | A brand new reading book | A prize for the best reader | *A rule that was used before and then stopped
exercise: «Scientists plan to reintroduce the lynx into the wild.» Which phrase means nearly the same as reintroduce into the wild? | *Set free in nature again | Keep in a zoo for ever | Move to a city | Hunt in the forest
test: «The farm will reintroduce old apple trees that had disappeared from the valley.» What does reintroduce mean here? | Sell the apples at the market | Cut down all the trees | Plant a new orchard for the first time | *Bring back to a place where they used to grow
test: «After the winter break, the club reintroduced the Friday spelling quiz.» What does reintroduced mean? | *Brought back into use | Taken away for ever | Made much harder | Given to new pupils only
exam: Which word means to bring back a rule that had stopped? | *reintroduce | interrupt | introduce | invent
